<Project>

  <!--
    中文：
      解决方案级的公共构建属性。所有项目自动继承本文件，无需逐个 csproj 重复。

      ★ 这里只放**对每个项目都成立**的设置。

        TargetFramework 刻意不放进来：Core 必须是 net8.0，而 Phase B 的
        ScannerHelper.Win32 与 ScannerHelper.App 必须是 net8.0-windows。这是
        整个架构最关键的一条边界（规格 §16），必须在各自的 csproj 里显式写明、
        一眼可见，而不是从一个公共文件里悄悄继承过来。

    English:
      Solution-wide build properties, inherited automatically by every project.

      Only settings true for *every* project belong here. TargetFramework is
      deliberately absent: Core must be net8.0 while Phase B's ScannerHelper.Win32
      and ScannerHelper.App must be net8.0-windows. That boundary is the most
      important one in the architecture (spec §16) and must be stated visibly in
      each csproj rather than inherited quietly from a shared file.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <!--
      中文：
        警告一律当作错误。

        测试计划的构建检查 B1 要求"零错误、零警告"，但在此之前没有任何东西
        强制它——全靠人在几十行构建输出里自己注意到。警告会累积：一旦容忍了
        第一条，后来的就淹没在噪音里，而可空性警告（CS8600 系列）恰恰是最
        值得当场处理的一类。Core 全程开启 <Nullable>enable</Nullable>，
        把这些警告放过去，等于把可空标注降级成了注释。

      English:
        Warnings are errors.

        Build check B1 in the test plan requires zero errors and zero warnings, but
        until now nothing enforced it — it relied on a person noticing amid dozens of
        lines of build output. Warnings accumulate: tolerate the first and later ones
        drown in the noise, and the nullability warnings (the CS8600 family) are
        exactly the kind worth handling on the spot. Core enables nullable reference
        types throughout, and letting those warnings pass would demote the
        annotations to comments.
    -->
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>

    <!--
      中文：
        确定性构建。相同的源码在不同机器上产出逐字节相同的程序集。

        规格 §22.1 要求发布版必须代码签名，而仓库 IT 会按**哈希**把可执行文件
        加进白名单。构建不确定意味着同一份源码重新构建一次哈希就变了，白名单
        随即失效，需要 IT 重新加一遍——那是要打电话找人的事。
      English:
        Deterministic builds: the same source produces byte-identical assemblies on
        any machine. Spec §22.1 requires the release to be code-signed, and warehouse
        IT allow-lists the executable *by hash*. Non-deterministic output means a
        rebuild of identical source changes the hash, invalidating the allow-list
        entry and requiring IT to add it again — a phone call, every time.
    -->
    <Deterministic>true</Deterministic>

    <!--
      中文：不生成隐式的 AssemblyInfo 冲突项；保持各项目自行声明元数据的自由。
      English: Keeps each project free to declare its own assembly metadata.
    -->
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>false</GenerateDocumentationFile>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
